* bl-a1-noisecancel: CG-CS noise-cancelling balun-LNA (single-in / diff-out).
* Lineage: Blaakmeer, Klumperink, Leenaerts, Nauta, "Wideband Balun-LNA with
* Simultaneous Output Balancing, Noise-Canceling and Distortion-Canceling",
* JSSC 2008 -- the canonical single-in/diff-out topology. Bench-v1 anchor.
* Structure-only, ZERO component values.
* Harness convention (diff3 3-port): port1 = single-ended RF in = VIN1;
* port2 = INVERTING output leg = VOUT1; port3 = NON-INVERTING output leg =
* VOUT2 (harness/diff3 net-name convention). Structure: input DC-blocked (C1)
* to shared node n1. CG path -- NM1 SOURCE at n1 (1/gm match), drain is the
* NON-INVERTING leg (in-phase): tuned load L2 to VDD, DC-blocked (C3) to
* VOUT2; NM1 gate AC-grounded by Cg. CS path -- NM2 GATE driven from n1
* through AC-couple Cin2 (own DC bias), drain is the INVERTING leg
* (anti-phase): tuned load L3 to VDD, DC-blocked (C4) to VOUT1. Published
* in-topology BIAS NETWORK (the paper's form): ONE current-mirror reference
* (R1 -> diode NM3) sets (a) the CG gate DC via feed R2, (b) the CS gate DC
* via feed R3, and (c) the CG-source BIAS CURRENT SINK NM4 (mirror output
* device from n1 to VSS -- the published current-source source-return).
* TRANSCRIPTION NOTE (logged): the first draft returned the CG source to VSS
* through an inductor; the 160-eval smoke showed a hard sds21 ceiling at
* -32 dB (l_max 12 nH = 69 ohm at 0.915 GHz shunts the shared input node).
* Replacing it with the PUBLISHED mirror-fed current-sink return (NM4) moved
* best sds21 to -8 dB. Bias-idiom slip fixed toward the published form.
* Approved 2026-09-14 (bench round 1, "approve all").
C C1 VIN1 n1
NMOS NM4 n1 n5 VSS VSS
NMOS NM1 n2 n4 n1 VSS
L L2 VDD n2
C C3 n2 VOUT2
C Cin2 n1 n6
NMOS NM2 n3 n6 VSS VSS
L L3 VDD n3
C C4 n3 VOUT1
R R1 VDD n5
NMOS NM3 n5 n5 VSS VSS
R R2 n5 n4
R R3 n5 n6
C Cg n4 VSS
